apparently some people missed the post by Izchak Miller about nethack
sources. Bill Randle (moderator - comp.sources.games) has made available
the sources to nethack 3.0h currently patched upto patchlevel 6. they
are available to uucp subscribers and by anon-ftp on uunet.uu.net in the
directory ~ftp/comp.sources.games/nethack3pl6/.... included in that
directory is the latest versions of ndmake, tmac.mn and patch (i think), etc.
the files were mostly compressed so binary transfers are needed.

anything interesting going on with the game? i can't fully play nh3.0h6
because there are hackers on my machine still finishing up nh3.0g5 games.
something i noticed about nh3.0h6 (BSD Unix HARD) was that in explore-mode
as a wizard character you could roll a wand of wishing with 3 charges in
your starting inventory (along with another wand!). it brought tears to
my eyes, if only that had been a normal game ...

curiously, what would you wish for first? second?? third??? fourth ...

